// `use` takes a dot-separated module path (constructs/use.c, research/010
// §12.1: `ImportPath ::= Identifier ("." Identifier)*`). The seed parses the
// declaration and discards it: the driver compiles exactly one file, so module
// resolution is deliberately not its job (research/011 §5.2).
//
// This case exists because nothing covered `use` at all. With no test to hold
// it in place the parser had drifted from its own grammar and matched `::`
// instead of `.`; Phase 2.2 adopted the dot form (see
// PHASE2_GAP_ANALYSIS.md App. B #6).
// EXPECT: 1
use std.io
use geometry.mesh
use a.b.c

let x = 1
print(x);
